      "text": "To find the value of \\( x \\) that satisfies \\( x^2 = 729 \\) given that \\( x \\) is positive, we need to take the positive square root of 729 since the problem specifies that \\( x \\) is positive.\n\nThe positive square root of 729 can be found by determining which number, when squared, equals 729. To find this, we can use the following steps:\n\n1. Start by looking at the perfect squares around 729:\n   \\[\n   20^2 = 400\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   21^2 = 441\n   \\]\n   Since 400 is less than 729 and 441 is greater than 729, the value of \\( x \\) must be between 20 and 21. Therefore, the positive square root of 729 is 21.\n\nThus, the value of \\( x \\) is \\( \\boxed{21} \\).",
